# Agent Infrastructure Enforcement

When you change **1+ files** under `.claude/` that are part of the canonical
agent infrastructure, or under `.codex/` / `.agents/` that are Codex runtime
adapters, run the `reviewing-agent-infrastructure` skill before reporting done.
Write a stamp to `.claude/hooks/state/agent-infrastructure.stamp.md`.

## Layer 1: This Rule (L2g — Advisory)

Tells you to validate. Fires when a glob-matched canonical or runtime-adapter
file is edited.

Skip for:
- `.claude/hooks/state/` and `.codex/hooks/state/` — runtime artifacts
  (stamps, hashes, scratchpads)
- `.claude/plans/` — descriptive plan documents, not infrastructure (no enforcement, no references)

## Layer 2: Stop Hook — Grind Loop (L5 — Enforced)

`post-task-check.sh` Check 6 verifies `agent-infrastructure.stamp.md` exists and is fresh (< 10 min). If missing, it exits 2 with a stderr blocker message so Claude is sent back. The grind-loop cap is 3 iterations; Claude Code's `stop_hook_active` flag prevents infinite re-firing.

## How to Validate

Follow the `reviewing-agent-infrastructure` skill checklist manually. Write a stamp to `.claude/hooks/state/agent-infrastructure.stamp.md`.

## Triggered Rule Notice

When this rule applies, mention it early:
"This touches agent infrastructure — agent-infrastructure validation will be required."
